.\" x11r63.sh.4 -- userland/packages/x11r6.3.  MIT, see LICENSE in userland/packages.
.TH X11R63.SH 4 "2026-10-31" "x11r63" "Amix add-on files"
.SH NAME
x11r63.sh \- X11R6.3's addition to the login environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /etc/profile.d/x11r63.sh
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B x11r63
package installs this file, which a login shell reads at the end of
.B /etc/profile
(see
.BR profile.d (4)).
It appends
.B /opt/amix/X11R6/bin
to
.B PATH
unless
.B PATH
already holds it or
.BR /usr/X11R6/bin ,
so X11R6.3's commands come after everything else on the path, and the
stock X11R4/R5 commands in
.B /usr/X/bin
keep their names wherever a profile puts them first.
Reading it twice changes nothing.
.PP
To leave X11R6.3 off a user's path, set
.B PATH
to include
.B /usr/X11R6/bin
in that user's own profile, or rename the file to
.BR x11r63.sh.off .
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /opt/amix/X11R6/bin
X11R6.3's commands, among them
.BR Xzz9000 ,
.BR xinit ,
.BR xdm ,
.B twm
and
.BR xterm .
.TP
.B /usr/X11R6
A link to
.BR /opt/amix/X11R6 .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR profile.d (4),
.BR Xamix (1),
.BR xinit (1)
